# Database backup operations

Lean prod may be a **single Docker MySQL** on the developer machine. App backups + MySQL binlog are complementary; neither replaces the other.

## What exists

| Mechanism | Location | Role |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Manual / UI backup | Maintenance → Database backups, `php artisan db:backup` | On-demand mysqldump + asset ZIP → `storage/backups/` |
| Scheduled backup | `routes/console.php` → scheduler container | Daily automated backup when `DB_BACKUP_SCHEDULE_ENABLED=true` |
| Retention purge | `php artisan db:backup:purge` | Weekly trim per retention policy |
| Plamod first-sync | `PlamodFirstSyncBackupService` | One-time backup before first Plamod sync |
| MySQL binlog | Docker MySQL config | Point-in-time / disaster recovery (ops-level, not app UI) |

## Default retention policy

Configured in `config/database_backup.php` (override via `.env`):

- **Recent window**: keep **every** backup from the last **14 days** (`DB_BACKUP_RETENTION_RECENT_DAYS`).
- **Weekly history**: for backups older than the recent window but within **180 days** (`DB_BACKUP_RETENTION_WEEKLY_DAYS`), keep **one backup per ISO week** (newest in each week).
- **Safety floor**: never purge below the **5** most recent backups (`DB_BACKUP_RETENTION_MINIMUM`), even if older than 180 days.

Purged backups: delete ZIP under `storage/backups/` and the `database_backups` row.

## Before destructive operations

Required on production-like DB **before**:

- `php artisan migrate` (or rollback)
- Migrations containing `Schema::drop` / table renames with data
- Bulk deletes or restore-from-backup drills

```powershell
php artisan db:backup --yes --description="Pre-migrate …" --created-by=system
php artisan migrate --pretend
```

Report the created backup filename in handoff when agents run migrations.

## Off-site copies (consolidation droplet)

- **Direction:** pricing-tool ZIPs **PC →** `134.209.213.143:/srv/stack/backups/offsite/pricing-tool/` only.
- **Never** push to `/srv/stack/backups/daily/` (that tree is pulled back to `Backups/ATA/`).
- Scripts in `local-llm/scripts/pricing-tool-backup-push-to-droplet.sh` + setup/cron installers.
- Docs: `local-llm/docs/server-consolidation/pricing-tool-offsite-backup.md`.

## Agent constraints

- Do **not** disable scheduled backups or retention without user approval.
- Do **not** run `db:backup:purge --yes` without `--dry-run` review unless user asked for purge.
- Do **not** imply backups exist — verify `database_backups` / `storage/backups/` or run backup first.
- Cross-reference `migration-data-safety.mdc` for migrate gates; autonomous migrate OK after backup per `operator-expectations.mdc`.

